/** \fn static IMPORT_C TInt Math::ATan(TReal &aTrg, const TReal &aSrcY, const TReal &aSrcX)
Calculates the angle between the x-axis and a line drawn from the origin to a point represented by its (x,y) co-ordinates.

The co-ordinates are passed as arguments to the function. This function returns the same result as arctan(y/x), but:

1. it adds +/-pi to the result, if x is negative

2. it sets the result to +/-pi/2, if x is zero but y is non-zero.

\param aTrg A reference containing the result in radians, a value between -pi exclusive and +pi inclusive.

\param aSrcY The y argument of the arctan(y/x) function.

\param aSrcX The x argument of the arctan(y/x) function.


<p><small>(generated from <a href="https://akawolf.org/documentation/pdk/GUID-1DB7AE7A-A505-3530-AC2B-EBAEFCD3F36A.html#GUID-4EB8A16C-075E-305E-AD76-ECFB085439C7">Symbian Developer Library</a>)</small></p>
*/

