/** \fn static IMPORT_C TInt Math::Mod(TReal &aTrg, const TReal &aSrc, const TReal &aModulus)
Calculates the modulo remainder.

This is the value of p mod q, the modulo remainder when dividing p by q. The result is given by p - q int (p/q): it has the same sign as p: thus, 5 mod 3 = 2, -5 mod 3 = -2. No error is raised if non-integer arguments are passed.

\param aTrg A reference containing the result.

\param aSrc The p argument to the mod function.

\param aModulus The q argument to the mod function.


<p><small>(generated from <a href="https://akawolf.org/documentation/pdk/GUID-1DB7AE7A-A505-3530-AC2B-EBAEFCD3F36A.html#GUID-226C05D5-7EB6-3181-B2C4-A822DFA0C438">Symbian Developer Library</a>)</small></p>
*/

